      "design": "r2B",
      "good": "Both identifiers and severity values remain on one line, making the lookup fields easy to scan.",
      "problems": "The narrow summary column produces short, choppy lines and a particularly tall first row. Large empty areas under the identifiers weaken the sense of each row as a unit.",
      "cause": "The 165px incident column preserves the full IDs, but leaves only 175px for the summary, of which 154px is usable text space."
    },
    {
      "design": "r2C",
      "good": "The wider summary column gives the prose more comfortable line lengths, while trace IDs and severity values remain intact.",
      "problems": "Incident IDs fragment across three lines, making their shared prefix prominent and their distinguishing suffixes harder to find. The added wrapping also makes the last row taller despite its short summary.",
      "cause": "The 110px incident column provides only 89px of text space; the 230px summary column gains space at the expense of the incident IDs."
    }
  ],
